WEBVTT

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.980
It's summer!

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.360
The beach.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.360
The villa!

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.370
Wow.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.920
It's wonderful!

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.970
I heard the post-Art Session 
party was held here,

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.050
but this place is great.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:32.920
Indeed.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.570
It's too hot.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:37.120
We should've stayed at the dorms.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.790
Right, Rin?

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.090
Why?

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:42.170
Tsukushi and Rin,

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.160
you should take off your armor

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.060
and enjoy the Hoshi Festival 
after party with us.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.850
Hibiki, get off me.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:49.820
You're making me hotter.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:51.580
Ow!

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.890
Rin, that seriously hurts. Stop.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.590
It's your fault for getting 
ahead of yourself.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.020
Right, Rin?

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.620
Hedgie, there's someone with 
a big head over here, too.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.290
I must enjoy summer more.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:09.460
You went all out.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:12.930
You do seem ready to play.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.230
This place hasn't changed.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.910
Hey, let's go to the beach.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:22.350
Todo-sensei, can we go swimming 
once we put our luggage away?

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:23.700
Sure.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.300
Tomorrow morning, we'll plant a memorial tree

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.750
to celebrate the success of your Art Session.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.980
Aside from that, you're 
free to enjoy yourselves.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.620
All right! Let's go have fun!

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.490
Yeah!

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:36.860
Roger that.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.490
We're going outside again?

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:41.450
Summer is calling.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:02:01.180
<b>Magic-Kyun Renaissance!</b>

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.960
A Heart-Pounding Summer Holiday

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.960
Tatewaki-senpai, here's the key.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.010
Thanks.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.230
Okay, guys.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.270
Let's get changed and meet at the beach.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:24.510
Okay.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.810
That's a big bag.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.300
Did you have it shipped?

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.230
Yeah.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.230
What on earth did you bring?

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.680
Clothes.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.360
He's always been a neat freak.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:38.960
He changes his clothes right 
away when he starts to sweat.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:43.740
That's why our closet is 
full of Tsukushi's clothes.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.120
How fashionable.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.870
Do I have to share a room 
with Hibiki here, too?

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.290
As long as we're here,

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.910
I'd like a different roommate for a change.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:59.510
Oh, right. Should we decide 
using a ghost leg lottery, then?

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.820
Something to write with.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:02.470
Wow.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.370
That was quick.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:05.970
Oh, it's a brush.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:09.340
What? Do you always carry 
that around with you?

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:12.210
I like ghost leg lotteries.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:15.980
Really? No wonder you did such a good job.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.900
Suminomiya, that's one 
beautiful ghost leg lottery.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.980
Thank you.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.490
Un, deux, trois...

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.090
There are only six.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:27.070
My little flower, you're not participating?

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.180
M-Me, too?

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.330
Anjo-senpai, she'll have her own room.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:35.140
I'm just kidding, Georgie.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:38.080
But how innocent of you to take me seriously.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.840
You're so cute.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.340
Please don't make fun of me.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.090
It's done. Choose your lines.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:45.590
Okay!

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.460
I'm this one.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:48.980
I was going to pick that one.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:51.220
I'll take whatever's left.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.370
The last one is lucky.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:54.980
My little flower, is this one yours?

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:55.740
What?

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:56.880
Anjo-senpai.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.730
Georgie, you're such a hothead.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:05.110
So how did we end up in the same room?

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.120
Look, Tsukushi. The view is amazing.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.370
Wow. It's sparkling.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.370
This should be good for today's snack.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:21.610
Rin Rin, do you think us adults 
were destined to room together?

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:23.020
You don't seem happy.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:26.380
I eat too many tasty 
foods when you're around.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.830
You're right.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.300
Suminomiya?

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.230
Are you okay?

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.570
I find confined spaces calming.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.450
You always have.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.990
You, too.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.750
You always came to get me.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:03.880
Hurry up and get changed.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.880
<i>Did my mom come here, too?</i>

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:23.350
Hello?

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:25.610
<i>Aigasaki-senpai, are you ready?</i>

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.160
<i>We're all waiting.</i>

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.660
Sorry. I'll be right there.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:36.410
Cherry, why don't you join us?

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.300
We're going to barbecue on the beach.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.290
Who's Cherry?

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.390
His name's Todo Chieri, 
so people call him Cherry.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:44.810
Ah.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:46.880
I'll pass.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.020
And don't call your teacher Cherry.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.050
Jeez. You kids...

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:59.060
Sorry. Thanks for waiting.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:03.140
Wow. My little flower, that's 
a wonderful swimsuit.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:07.070
Senpai, that color looks great on you.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.180
Yeah.

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:10.700
It's exciting because it's not 
what you normally wear.

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:12.620
I-I'm not...

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.950
It's cute.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.860
Too bright.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:18.890
Guys, stop staring.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.750
You're upsetting Hana-chan-senpai.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:26.050
Oh, um... th-thanks.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.020
We can't help it.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:32.640
Beautiful flowers shine even more 
brightly when they're adored.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:33.180
What?

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.300
Hey, Anjo-senpai.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.520
You're exuding too many sexy pheromones.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:38.860
Try to control yourself.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:39.890
What?

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:43.190
Yeah, we should be enjoying 
each other's company today.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.930
Right, Ichijoji?

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.060
You're right.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.250
No objections.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:48.940
Yeah.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:50.590
Roger that.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:54.070
It's been a while, but 
maybe I'll go swimming.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:58.620
Sure, Angelo. I'll race 
you to that pointy rock!

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:04.690
Alright, but don't 
underestimate my sexy freestyle.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.560
Hold up!

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.880
They call me the Flying Fish of Hoshinomori.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.260
Who does?

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:14.220
What a coincidence. That's 
what they call me, too.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.010
Seriously?

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:18.140
Two flying fishes?

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:20.450
All right! Let's go, guys!

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.140
Yeah!

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:28.850
<i>The sparkling light is bursting</i>

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:30.370
<i>Don't you know? Don't you know?</i>

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:34.570
<i>You're too bright and beautiful!</i>

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:40.410
<i>We still haven't noticed the 
magic you hold in your hand</i>

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:46.210
<i>The words "you're not alone" 
change everything</i>

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:52.380
<i>The world starts to shine as 
it's reflected in your eyes</i>

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:57.840
<i>Pouring forth are dream-like 
and miraculous moments</i>

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:10.940
<i>My princess (we met)
 let me protect you (always)</i>

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.220
Friends

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:21.080
<i>I'm so obsessed with your brilliant 
smile, it's making me dizzy</i>

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:25.410
<i>Don't you know? (I'm your prisoner)</i>

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:31.250
<i>Before I knew it, I was drawn to you and I 
want to hold you so much, I can't help myself</i>

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:37.130
<i>You're beautiful (so bright 
you're beautiful!)</i>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.590
<i>Don't you know? Don't you know?</i>

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:42.930
<i>You're too bright and beautiful!</i>

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:48.780
<i>You're mine and I'm yours</i>

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:54.110
I'm stuffed. I couldn't eat another bite.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.160
That was good, Rintaro.

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.570
Really?

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:59.320
Except for the carrots.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.980
I thought you'd eat them if I mixed them in,

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:04.080
but I guess it didn't work.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:08.080
Tatewaki-senpai, I loved everything.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.490
Hibiki, you're such a good 
boy for eating everything.

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:14.590
But in contrast, Monet... Unbelievable.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:17.450
Hey, Rintaro, shut up.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:18.760
Right, Rin?

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:25.310
Tatewaki-senpai, sorry for 
making you cook for us again.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:26.600
Thank you.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.650
It's fine.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:31.730
I'm happy as long as I get 
to see you guys smile.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.770
That was the first time I had grilled clams.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:37.490
They were good.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:38.880
Right?

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:42.160
And wasn't that your first time at the beach?

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:42.850
Yeah.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:43.870
Seriously?

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:50.000
Teika, I think that was your first 
time being buried in the sand, too.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.010
Yeah.

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.510
Are you blushing?

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:56.490
That's great.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:58.130
I'm not so sure.

00:10:58.130 --> 00:10:59.710
Sure it was.

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:02.510
My little flower,

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:05.890
we're meeting again tonight for fireworks.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:07.640
Okay.

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:12.740
That should do it.

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:21.480
What is that?

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:32.920
<i>Sparkles?</i>

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.370
Aigasaki?

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.930
Todo-sensei.

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:51.550
For you.

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:53.120
Magic-Kyun!

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:56.480
Magic-Kyun.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.050
Renaissance.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.510
Todo-sensei.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:05.200
This is the Light of Arte, isn't it?

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:06.740
Yeah.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:11.710
Only those who participated in successful 
Art Sessions can enter this place.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:13.590
Art Sessions?

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.590
My mother's flowers.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:24.220
You can tell?

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:26.030
Yes.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.410
I see.

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:40.420
I was going to tell you tomorrow

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.360
when I brought you here to 
plant your memorial tree.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:47.480
I told you once before that the 
year she chaired the committee,

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:50.120
the festival was known as the Summer 
Festival of Miracles and Blessings.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:51.350
Yes.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:55.690
I was on the Hoshi Festival 
committee then, too.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:58.250
The Hoshi Festival committee?

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:02.860
Sakura-san was two years ahead of me.

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:05.720
I see.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:08.110
I didn't know that.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:09.470
I'm kind of happy to hear it.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:12.720
You really are her daughter.

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:13.660
What?

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:18.230
You look directly at people 
and smile just like she did.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:19.980
Really?

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.130
And the way you always see something through

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:25.390
once you've set your mind to it.

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:26.790
Oh, I'm not...

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:31.130
When we ran into a wall and nearly 
gave up on the Art Session,

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:35.080
she told us, "I know we can do it."

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:40.290
If you're ever unsure, 
it's okay to stand still.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.600
But, even if we're struggling,

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:45.630
as long as we keep trying,

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:46.630
I know we can do it.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.390
That's what I believe.

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:52.510
Her words gave us courage,

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:55.570
and we successfully 
completed the Art Session.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.900
At the very least, that's what I thought.

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:02.040
Later we planted a memorial tree together.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:05.910
I haven't been back here since.

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.160
It's a peach tree!

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:15.750
Wow, there are so many!

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:18.420
It's grown.

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:23.200
When I had fevers as a child,

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:25.550
my mother would peel peaches for me.

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:28.300
The fevers were painful,

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:31.830
but I liked eating peaches.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.310
When I met Sakura-san,

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.510
she gave me a peach, too.

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:39.810
Really?

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:42.810
Right after I was chosen
 for the Hoshi Festival committee.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:44.820
For some reason,

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:48.850
no matter how many times I tried, I 
couldn't produce the Light of Arte.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:53.250
That's when I saw her making 
flower arrangements.

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:08.800
She was so engrossed in the flowers,

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:12.590
I could tell she felt 
compelled to arrange them.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:30.680
I'm sorry. Thank you.

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.740
You can keep that if you'd like.

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:46.510
Sensei?

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:48.500
Oh, right.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:54.220
The days I spent with Sakura-san and 
the others were truly wonderful.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.140
They were miraculous times.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:58.000
Miraculous...

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:02.840
While watching your Art Session, 
I remembered those feelings.

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:09.150
I hope we can meet here again as adults.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:16.000
By the time this little peach tree 
bears fruit, what will we be doing?

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:21.410
I made it to this day without 
keeping that promise.

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:24.010
But this tree didn't forget.

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:26.670
It grew and produced fruit.

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:35.430
Mom, I'm taking a few flowers.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:40.430
Sensei.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:42.680
Thank you.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:17:01.290
I'm glad to have heard a story 
about my mother that I didn't know.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.610
No, thank you.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:08.770
Sure.

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:16.930
Hey!

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:20.060
Senpai, the fireworks display is starting.

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:22.070
Okay.

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:23.200
Aigasaki.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:23.810
Yes?

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:27.810
You should treasure the 
feelings you have right now.

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:29.810
I will.

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:32.820
Cherry, why don't you join us?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:33.980
I'll pass.

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:35.880
And don't call me Cherry.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.130
Okay.

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:38.960
See you later.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:39.950
Excuse us.

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:47.580
It's about time I started walking, too.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:58.490
All right! Let's get this 
fireworks display started!

00:17:58.490 --> 00:17:59.720
Yeah!

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:02.710
This is my first time 
lighting fireworks, too.

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:05.050
Sumi, this day has been 
full of firsts for you.

00:18:05.050 --> 00:18:07.140
Tomorrow let's go out to the point.

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:08.980
There's a lighthouse there.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.310
A lighthouse?

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:13.060
You like lighthouses, right?

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:13.680
Yeah.

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:15.250
I'm impressed, Georgie-senpai.

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:16.740
You know him well.

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:18.320
Mouse?

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.410
Rin is a hedgehog.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:23.000
Get it right, Sumi-senpai.

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:25.410
That's right. Here.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:29.750
Hana-chan-senpai!

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:32.960
Be careful.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.170
S-Sorry.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:37.460
It's not your fault.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.800
It was Rintaro.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:39.930
Me?

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.750
Sorry.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:44.260
You should apologize to Hana-chan-senpai.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:45.520
Sorry.

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:53.690
It's beautiful.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.660
Our Art Session was beautiful, too.

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:00.660
Yeah. It was great.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:03.660
It sure was fun.

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:05.940
Yeah.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:09.150
We made some nice memories.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:12.670
Because of you, Georgie. Thanks.

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:15.800
No, because of all of us.

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:32.560
It's sad once the party is over.

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.690
Yeah.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:39.360
Once today is over, we'll 
go our separate ways.

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:40.500
No.

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:43.570
What? Oh, um...

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:49.520
It was a miracle we met in the first place.

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:51.960
I'd like to spend some more time together.

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:54.590
You're right.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:59.210
I bet we could do even more 
if we worked together.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:01.140
Yeah.

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:04.090
Way to go, my little flower. Nicely said.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:09.180
Yeah, but what are we going to do 
now that the Hoshi Festival is over?

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:16.900
A shooting star.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.710
What? Where?

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.440
It's gone.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:23.240
One more, please. I'd like to see one.

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:26.610
Should we wish for us to stay together?

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:31.500
Georgie, did you think of something?

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:42.950
All right. It's done.

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:47.070
I hope it gets bigger.

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:49.370
As big as this peach tree.

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:50.810
How many years will that take?

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:55.300
We've planted our memorial tree, and our roles
 on the Hoshi Festival committee have ended.

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:57.170
Good work, everyone.

00:20:57.170 --> 00:21:01.320
But, I believe each of us has a new goal.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:07.570
Going forward, we'd like to form 
a Hoshigei event committee.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:09.650
Huh? What?

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:10.450
Todo-sensei.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:12.950
Please be our advisor.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:14.760
What?

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:17.600
But I was finally released 
from watching over you guys.

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:18.580
What are you talking about?

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:20.660
Can't you make an exception?

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:22.740
Please!

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.440
What a pain in the butt.

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:25.640
That's not my problem.

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:27.780
Cherry, did you just smile?

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:28.590
Yeah.

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:30.200
Which means...

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.430
I didn't smile! And don't call me Cherry!

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:34.560
What do you say?

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:38.190
Fine.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:41.820
I'll at least let the principal 
know what you want to do.

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:43.350
He said it's okay!

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:44.690
All right!

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:46.730
That's not what I meant!

00:21:46.730 --> 00:21:50.280
Don't stop listening until 
I'm finished talking!

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:28.710
If it's what she wants, 
I'd even become a prince.

00:23:28.710 --> 00:23:30.760
I'm all the prince she needs.

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:31.630
Then let's settle this in a contest!

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:34.370
Next time on Magic-Kyun! Renaissance:

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>You Are the Prince of Destiny</b>

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:36.440
"You Are the Prince of Destiny."

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:38.050
Once we're princes, you'll be...

00:23:38.050 --> 00:23:38.810
Magic-Kyun!

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:39.940
For us, right?
